# NOTICE

superred-target-hackaprompt

This module is a port of HackAPrompt's level defenses into the superred
red-teaming framework. Original code in this module (the superred adaptation: the
target, completer, factory, and tests) is licensed MIT (see LICENSE). It
reproduces the level prompt templates and input filters from HackAPrompt; the
upstream MIT license text is preserved in `LICENSES/HackAPrompt-MIT.txt`.

## Upstream: HackAPrompt

- Project: HackAPrompt — "Ignore This Title and HackAPrompt: Exposing Systemic
  Vulnerabilities of LLMs through a Global Prompt Hacking Competition"
- Repository: https://github.com/PromptLabs/hackaprompt (commit f0a035a)
- Paper: Schulhoff et al., EMNLP 2023 (arXiv:2311.16119).
- License: MIT — Copyright (c) 2023 hackaprompt team

### Ported verbatim (level defenses)

`src/hackaprompt_target/_vendor/levels.py` is a byte-faithful port of the 11 level
`format_prompt` templates (upstream `hackaprompt/evaluator.py` `Level*Evaluator`)
and the input-filter defenses (`hackaprompt/utils.py`: `contains_blacklisted_word`,
`contains_pwned_letters`, `remove_non_emoji`). Every level's prompt was verified
byte-identical to upstream. Kept under `_vendor` (ruff-excluded) so the upstream
text is preserved exactly.

### Ported logic (MIT)

`target.py` orchestrates each level (filter/escape → model call → Level 6's second
turn) and `completer.py` reaches the model via litellm. The upstream completer
(pre-1.0 OpenAI SDK + a FlanT5 HF space), the MongoDB game DB, and the Gradio UI
are NOT ported. Deviations are documented in `ASSUMPTIONS.md`.

